tonight parents will meet in what they  call a movement to break up ccsd  this comes a week after the district  opened up in-person learning  through the hybrid model madison  kimbrough has the latest from henderson  yes tonight's meeting is a call to  action urging governor sysolak to change  the way the district is organized  something parents say has been an issue  for several decades  the goal is for the district to be  broken up to more localized school  districts instead of one massive one  ccsd is the fifth largest in the nation  with over 320 thousand students  with the amount of kids in the district  parents claim it makes it hard to manage  which is why many believe so many  students haven't returned fully back to  the classroom  jenny lynn eddington who used to have  her two children in the clark county  school district explains  we will be meeting together and rolling  out a strategy  to let sisalak governor sisolak know  what we're asking of him  we want him to know that we're not  satisfied being  among the worst states for education  we're not satisfied with that and we  feel that if  there was a smaller school district then  we would be able to  solve some of the problems and the  problems would be managed  better and we could have gotten the kids  back full time  safely more earlier than they have been  eddington and several other parents have  created a facebook group where they post  about their next events  and plans moving forward so far since  starting a couple weeks ago  the public facebook group known as  breakup ccsd  has already gained thousands of  followers and tonight's meeting is  expected to bring 80 to 100 parents and  that starts at 6 30 tonight  reporting in henderson madison kimbrough  8 news now
 

